<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Examples for Derived Questions in Probing Analysis.</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present qualitative examples of derived questions used in our probing analysis.
These questions focus on the same visual regions as the original queries while varying the queried attributes to examine the semantic consistency of latent representations. During probing analysis, the obtained latent embeddings and these derived questions are presented to the model for final answer generation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.22766v1/image6.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A1.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The derived questions focus on the same region or object as the original question, while differing in the queried attribute aspects.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
